.TH "SECURITYPOLICYVIOLATIONEVENT.COLUMNNUMBER" "3JS" "April 3, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SecurityPolicyViolationEvent.columnNumber \-
SecurityPolicyViolationEvent: columnNumber property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]columnNumber\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]SecurityPolicyViolationEvent\f[R] interface is the character
position in the source file line of the document or worker script at
which the Content Security Policy (CSP) violation occurred.
.PP
This property is used with the
\f[CR]SecurityPolicyViolationEvent.sourceFile\f[R] and
\f[CR]SecurityPolicyViolationEvent.lineNumber\f[R] properties, which
together provide the exact location in the source that caused the
violation.
.SH VALUE
A number representing the character position number where the violation
occurred.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
document.addEventListener(\(dqsecuritypolicyviolation\(dq, (e) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(e.columnNumber);
});
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CSPViolationReport.columnNumber\f[R]
